  <Properties>
    <hideFromXmlSitemap>
      <Value><![CDATA[0]]></Value>
    </hideFromXmlSitemap>
    <mainContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "fcc8e419-7aff-4851-8e90-01e818ee2fa7",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Accessibility"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EAccessibility refers to the design, construction, development and maintenance of environments in a way that ensures they can be used by as many people as possible, including those with disabilities.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "accessibility"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "30ad1bb0-b5b1-496f-b24c-b837e532ebe4",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Active frontage"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Active frontage"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EActive frontage refers to the design of buildings and spaces along streets or public areas in such a way that promotes engagement, interaction and activity at the ground level.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "42c5701b-5eee-4da0-916e-abd1bc61067c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Active travel"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EActive travel refers to modes of transportation that involve physical activity, such as walking or cycling, as the primary means of getting from one place to another.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Active travel"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "648306da-cbc5-47c1-9b90-f7faf9e96697",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Adaptive cycling"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Adaptive cycling"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EAdaptive cycling refers to using specialised equipment or bicycle modifications to make them accessible to individuals with varying abilities.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b05c05c4-50f4-4cf8-8287-41e27513299c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Amenity"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Amenity"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EAmenity is a feature of a place that is useful, desirable, or pleasant, contributing to the comfort, enjoyment, and quality of life for its users, residents, or visitors.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ade37ccb-29cd-47a4-8090-c0564757f530",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Appraisal"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Appraisal"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe assessment of the physical environment, character, assets and restrictions of a site and its surroundings.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f3bb12e9-6918-4acf-b450-db6a2373f12c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Backland development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Backland development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBackland development refers to building on land located behind the rear building line of existing structures, often in garden areas or vacant plots that are not visible from main roads and are typically accessed from a side or rear road.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "3f6f5393-4212-48a8-a269-7b7e85e12c6e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Banding design"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Banding design"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBanding design consists of a decorative band across the top of a building that projects beyond the wall, also known as a cornice.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "bb87cf7a-a6ed-4e0e-add5-86e884836be2",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Basin"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Basin"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA ground depression that is normally dry, designed to store surface water and provide attenuation prior to discharge.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "7b7dc47d-a9f9-4fc0-88e0-1a925cda548f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Biodiversity"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Biodiversity"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBiodiversity is defined as the variety of plants and animals living within an area or habitat, with different habitats contributing different functions or services for our environment.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "18e673dc-5945-4190-9485-090b37af03f7",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBiodiversity net gain is an approach which aims to leave the natural environment in a measurably better state than before. Net gain delivers measurable improvements for biodiversity by creating or enhancing habitats in association with development, which can be achieved preferably on-site, off-site or through a combination of on-site and off-site measures.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ab4ca5d8-6f44-4d55-90b7-7aff6e4c1bed",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Bio-retention area"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Bio-retention area"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA bio-retention area is a type of sustainable drainage system (SuDS). It typically consists of a shallow depression with engineered soil layers, vegetation, mulch and sometimes an under-drain system.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b8554a26-dd30-455a-8b31-9666b3bfe69e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Block size (urban)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Block size (urban)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA block is a defined area of land within a settlement that is bounded by streets or other physical boundaries. It is the basic unit of urban land use and typically consists of a collection of buildings.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ad1012a3-4a1b-49d5-aeb6-daa20b83a6c1",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Blue infrastructure (networks)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Blue infrastructure (networks)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBlue infrastructure usually relates to urban water infrastructure, including ponds, lakes, streams rivers and storm water provision.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "36dc9ecb-1e99-4407-980f-d5c5d42637c2",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Boundary treatment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Boundary treatment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EMeans by which areas are enclosed including but not limited to fencing, railing, walls, hedges and other vegetation.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b94e52d0-42c9-48b0-bc69-2084455aa6aa",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Building line"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Building line"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA building line is the line formed by the frontages of buildings along a street.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b02f3c7c-5f8d-4825-9995-876a8d6cf43d",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Built form"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Built form"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBuilt form refers to the physical characteristics, layout and arrangement of buildings, structures and other constructed elements within a particular area or built environment.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "e3547ed1-ec6b-47cf-b217-1655155b6bc3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Change of use"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Change of use"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EChange of use refers to altering the designated purpose of a building or land from one use class to another, such as converting a shop into a residential dwelling. If the change is considered \u201Cmaterial,\u201D it signifies a substantial change in the property\u2019s purpose that affects the local area, potentially requiring planning permission from the local planning authority (LPA).\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "348a0fe1-0bfc-4c38-9a5f-ebebb8746834",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Character"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Character"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ECharacter refers to the distinctive and unique qualities that define the identity, atmosphere and overall feel of a specific area or locality. It encompasses a combination of physical, cultural, historical and social attributes that give a place its sense of personality, charm and authenticity.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "cede9357-2903-4018-b6f4-420201caa8a0",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Climate change (adaptation and mitigation)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Climate change (adaptation and mitigation)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EClimate change adaptation is the process of adjusting natural or human systems to respond to current or expected impacts of climate change, aiming to reduce harm or take advantage of new opportunities. Climate change mitigation is action taken to lessen the impact of human activities on the climate, mainly by cutting greenhouse gas emissions.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b0e9915e-a0f0-4487-8a49-84fb7a1c0703",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Clustering"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Clustering"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EClustering: refers to the spatial grouping of buildings or housing units that share common characteristics, such as tenure type or target demographic which are closely sited to one another and not spread out.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ba26017d-81f9-47b3-acb7-545c03e4a11d",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Context"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Context"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA building or site context usually refers to the surrounding physical environment, but can also refer to the social, economic and political nature of a place.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f5c4bed3-3097-4de7-87fc-2249112de1ce",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Conservation area"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Conservation area"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESection 69 of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990 places a duty on every local planning authority to determine which parts of their area are areas of special architectural or historic interest, the character or appearance of which it is desirable to preserve or enhance. Such areas can then be designated as conservation areas.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "49c9fe5f-e24c-4470-b8f7-b29336b5e1d3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Conservation area appraisal"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Conservation area appraisal"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA conservation area appraisal is a document prepared by local authorities to assess the special architectural and historic interest of a designated conservation area\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "961fe28c-d777-4a28-a9b3-3addb874014e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Copenhagen-style crossing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Copenhagen-style crossing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA Copenhagen style crossing, or continuous pavement crossing, extends the pavement and cycleway across a minor side road junction, creating a level surface where vehicles must give way to pedestrians and cyclists. This design slows traffic, provides an uninterrupted route for pedestrians and cyclists, and visually signals to drivers that they are entering a pedestrian priority zone. This is achieved by including ramps, markings, colouration of surfaces, and by ensuring that the corners are relatively tight.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f7e743e5-c42b-4785-9131-72d2cefc2a17",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Copings or coping stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Copings or coping stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ECopings is the capping or covering of a wall. A splayed or wedge coping is one that slopes in a single direction; a saddle coping slopes to either side of a central high point.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ad39c6a0-ffce-4af5-a029-3304ad13a9b4",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Corbel or corbelling"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Corbel or corbelling"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA corbel or corbelling is an architectural element that projects from a wall and is used to support a structure above it, such as a beam, arch, balcony or cornice.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "64147c62-0919-4782-be75-0e60c68716c7",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Coursed stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Coursed stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStonework laid in regular horizontal layers (courses), where stones are of uniform height. This technique provides a neat, structured appearance and is common in traditional masonry.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "11ebe469-0b0d-4540-b36f-359a74a92059",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Design and Access Statement (DAS)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Design and Access Statement (DAS)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EDesign and Access Statements should clearly detail the access and highway issues related to the development proposal, in accordance with the Local Plan policies and the Street Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "379c46fd-bbee-4e21-aa32-787e92882c26",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Design process (planning)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Design process (planning)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe design process in planning refers to the structured approach taken by a design team to develop a project, from concept to completion, by breaking it down into stages to ensure quality and meet project goals. This involves analysing requirements, exploring solutions, developing detailed plans, and often following frameworks like the RIBA Plan of Work to guide the process and manage deliverables. For development projects, it is integrated with the planning system to achieve well-designed places.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "3543ec4e-307c-4924-988f-e917f8e37c46",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Detailing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Detailing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EDetailing refers to the specific design elements, features and ornamentation that are incorporated into the construction of a building or structure.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1f8b61d1-65c5-4920-bd69-53a9e9f5ae9c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Development plan"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Development plan"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA development plan sets out the Council\u2019s planning policies for securing growth, investment, sustainable development and improving the environment in the district. The policies seek to improve economic, social and environmental well-being, delivering successful places, businesses and people.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "75258f56-3526-4260-ac59-f0d44f25da4d",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Dormer"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Dormer"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA dormer is an architectural feature that projects from a sloped roof, typically containing a window or windows and often having its own small roof.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "c76cedaf-16f5-4c48-9d48-9439aa085831",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Dwellings per hectare (dph)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Dwellings per hectare (dph)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EDwellings per hectare (dph) measures the number of homes that can ft into a given area of land, with higher (dph) indicating more homes and higher density. The specific (dph) target for a new development depends on factors like its location, proximity to transport, and local policy, with common targets ranging from 20 to 40 (dph) for greener environments, and to over 50 (dph) in urban centres.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "584d882e-1491-4453-a831-f4ec26f498f3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Eaves"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Eaves"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe lowest, overhanging part of a sloping roof.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "934038e1-81cb-4818-83a4-ac847a993fc0",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Electric vehicle (EV) charging"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Electric vehicle (EV) charging"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EElectric vehicle (EV) charging refers to the process of supplying electrical energy to recharge the batteries of electric vehicles.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "82042077-96d1-4c7b-abeb-d38dd9a4e3dd",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Enclosure"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Enclosure"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EEnclosure refers to the creation of defined spaces or boundaries within the built environment. These spaces are typically formed by buildings, walls or landscaping elements.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "68e4658c-9c10-4541-9638-18c8af6e7ca1",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Enclosure ratio"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Enclosure ratio"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EEnclosure ratio is an urban design principle that compares the height of buildings to the width of the street or public space that they define. Creating a sense of enclosure can create different visual qualities of space, whilst impacting on the user\u2019s perception of comfort.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d193544d-4df0-4f6d-ac51-bf867827291e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Environmental impact (assessment)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Environmental impact (assessment)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EAn environmental impact assessment is a process required for certain projects to ensure that decisions consider any likely significant effects on the environment.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d377713f-7846-461f-b8fa-8b32ee2c684d",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Fa\u00E7ade"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Facade"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA fa\u00E7ade is the external face or front of a building, often designed to be decorative or to express the architectural style of the structure.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "5c29a430-15e8-4430-85d2-4a459eceea64",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Fascia"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Fascia"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA fascia is an architectural term that refers to a horizontal board or band located along the edge of a roof. It is typically mounted where the roof meets the outer walls of the building.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "286dcc88-0bec-4b95-9411-af16edd71ce0",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Fenestration"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Fenestration"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFenestration refers to the arrangement, design and placement of windows, doors and other openings in a building\u2019s fa\u00E7ade or envelope.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "c9e79d4e-99c5-474b-90ac-0f3c0fbf7220",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Filter strips"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Filter strips"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFilter strips are areas of vegetation, typically grass or other native plants, planted alongside water bodies, drainage channels or agricultural fields.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "6c535163-f864-473a-8bd9-a529c7072bae",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Formulated design"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Formulated design"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EFormulated design refers to the process of developing and articulating a clear design concept, that guides a projects layout, form and appearance.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1cb1be44-703b-440b-80df-715e7fe3bed5",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Gable"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Gable"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA gable is an architectural feature commonly found on the ends of pitched or sloping roofs. It typically forms a triangular shape and is created by the intersection of two roof slopes, with the highest point or peak of the gable called the \u201Cridge\u201D.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "83f4c8e4-f47a-4103-913c-add8c53c3e2e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Gateway"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Gateway"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA feature such as trees, lighting, public art, or a particularly designed building that marks the entrance to a distinct area.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "e093377b-5245-43be-972d-ede4d33887f2",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Gentle density"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Gentle density"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EGentle density is an urban design concept that focuses on increasing the density of neighbourhoods in a gradual and incremental manner, while preserving the character, scale and quality of the built environment.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "0d906681-12b0-4041-9209-d651a979cf20",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green belt"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green belt"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EGreen Belt refers to land designated around certain towns and cities to prevent urban sprawl by keeping land permanently open. Development can only take place if certain exceptions apply or it has been demonstrated \u2018very special circumstances\u2019 exist.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1efeab53-2fb7-4870-949d-af3cf58fc731",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green buffer"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green buffer"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA green buffer is a vegetated area, typically consisting of trees, shrubs, grasses and other vegetation, that serves as a barrier or transitional zone between different land uses or natural areas.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "694bd7ff-6499-4b48-956d-1b3da86209ae",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green corridor"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green corridor"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA green corridor is a linear or interconnected network of vegetated areas, such as parks, grass verges, street trees or natural habitats, that are strategically planned and managed to facilitate ecological connectivity, biodiversity conservation and sustainable urban development.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "28edcde2-ffc9-49cd-879c-85bec79110d8",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green infrastructure (networks)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green infrastructure (networks)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EGreen infrastructure has traditionally been perceived as a combination of spatial or linear environmental assets including open green space, amenity space, landscape planting, urban parks and gardens, commons and village greens. Natural and semi-natural wildlife habitat such as woodland and heath, country parks, Registered Parks \u0026amp; Gardens, Scheduled Monuments, Local Nature Reserves, Sites of Special Scientific Interest, Local Wildlife Sites, church grounds and cemeteries, allotments, playing fields and sports pitches, public rights of way, the Trans Pennine Trail and other recreational routes.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d5d446c3-e4e5-4e9a-b402-713303f95acb",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green roof"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green roof"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA green roof is a building roof that is partially or completely covered with vegetation and a growing medium, planted over a waterproof membrane.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "4b267bec-7802-4a27-bafc-51ba087dcb8b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green space / open space"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green space / open space"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPublicly accessible land in any ownership which can include country parks, natural areas, sports and recreation grounds, urban parks and amenity open space including cemeteries, mown grass and planted areas and playgrounds for example.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "de483864-7a99-4aee-86f8-e737ea5a3d26",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green wall"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Green wall"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA green wall is a wall partially or completely covered with vegetation, which includes a growing medium, such as soil, substrate or hydroponics, and an integrated water delivery system.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "11bb7b77-b00a-4260-ae29-2873a7bd3977",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Habitable room"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Habitable room"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA habitable room is a space within a dwelling primarily used for living, sleeping, or dining, excluding areas like bathrooms, toilets, corridors, and utility rooms. However, there is no single legal definition, and the exact meaning can vary depending on the specific planning context, such as calculating residential density or assessing a proposal\u2019s impact on daylight and privacy.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b6684659-ed01-45b0-8eec-ef1be4d46307",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Habitats"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Habitats"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EHabitats are defined as the natural environments or homes where plants, animals, and other organisms live, providing them with the resources needed for survival, such as food, water, shelter, and air. These habitats can be vast, like forests and oceans, or very small, such as under a stone, and are classified into different types like terrestrial (land), freshwater, and marine. The UK has a specific classification system for its habitats, including priority habitats, to guide conservation efforts.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "e987381d-03ec-4c5b-a9ca-169fba594dc0",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Hard landscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Hard landscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EHard landscape refers to the non-living elements of a landscape design such as paving and surfacing, walls and fences, structures, water features, outdoor furniture, edging and borders, lighting, sculptures and art.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "23884e5e-b78c-4940-911d-6f697c86fd14",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Heritage"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Heritage"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EHeritage refers to the legacy of physical artifacts and intangible attributes inherited from past generations, maintained in the present, and preserved for the benefit of future generations.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "2b80fb04-638a-468e-a87a-3f7e1d281827",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Heritage asset or assets"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Heritage asset or assets"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA heritage asset or assets can consist of a building, site, area or landscape with heritage significance that should be considered in planning decisions. This includes both designated assets and those identified by the local planning authority, such as locally listed buildings.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d61211b2-c253-401b-94da-49d3e806330c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "High-density housing (development)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "High-density housing (development)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EHigh-density housing refers to residential developments that accommodate a large number of housing units or people within a relatively small area of land. This housing style typically involves multi-story apartment buildings, condos, or closely spaced town homes where units share common walls, floors, or ceilings.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "aaa9d2cd-3b4a-491b-8e74-911aeb37a425",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Historic environment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Historic environment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe term \u2018historic environment\u2019 includes Registered Parks and Gardens, Historic Landscapes, Historic Battle Sites, Conservation Areas, Scheduled Monuments and archaeological sites.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f6c2767a-0f47-4add-a74f-3dbe68285609",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Housing our ageing population panel for innovation (HAPPI)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Housing our ageing population panel for innovation (HAPPI)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe HAPPI principles are based on 10 key design criteria. Many are recognisable from good design generally - good light, ventilation, room to move around and good storage, but they have relevance to the spectrum of older persons\u2019 housing which needs to both offer an attractive alternative to the family home and be able to adapt over time to meet changing needs.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "a7655e7c-6628-4366-9952-f58779fdfba2",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Housing type / typology"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Housing type / typology"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EHousing type / typology refers to the classification or categorisation of different types of residential buildings or dwellings based on common characteristics such as architectural design, layout, size, form and function.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "383b3441-b66f-497f-bbee-8c4e23d4249e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Identity"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Identity"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EIdentity encompasses a place\u2019s unique physical features, historical heritage, distinct cultural traditions, shared social practices, and the personal emotional connections residents have to the area. It is shaped by the combination of architecture, landscape, and community stories, and provides a sense of belonging, continuity, and local pride for its residents.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "5e345fa5-f97d-46c9-8b0c-37afb50c9fcb",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Inclusive (design)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Inclusive (design)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EInclusive describes something that includes a wide range of people, practices, or items, ensuring no one is excluded. Inclusive design ensures that places and experiences are open to all people, regardless of age, disability and background.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1e409149-68e1-4e02-b80c-7c688128f5f1",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Infill development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Infill development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EDevelopment which takes place on vacant, underused or undeveloped land between existing built areas.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "a82a4918-d33c-448d-9628-5566a618912f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Infiltration"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Infiltration"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe passage of surface water into the ground.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "7c68eb5a-989e-46de-aa39-98e813ced8bf",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Interception (storage)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Interception (storage)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe prevention and capture (storage) of runoff from the site for the majority of small (frequent) rainfall events (or for the initial depth of rainfall for larger events).\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "50fbbef9-738a-4c4f-8c38-25025b67966e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Kneeler"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Kneeler"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA large, often decorative stone placed at the base of a gable end, where the sloping roof meets the horizontal wall. Kneelers help support the coping and visually anchor the gable.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "81ef4ce5-d759-49a8-a454-e4da70c83401",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Landmark"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELandmark buildings are defined as those that stand out from their immediate and surrounding context by virtue of their design, size, or other characteristics (i.e. mark a key gateway or vista into the city centre and include distinctive/illuminating features of special interest).\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b3a2705f-39f1-4f26-b118-e18d71e4edb6",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Landscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Landscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELandscape refers to the visible features of an area of land, including natural elements such as terrain, vegetation, bodies of water, and climate, as well as human-made elements such as buildings, roads and infrastructure.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "89ce395a-3f8d-4df5-8b70-92fb81864bf9",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Landscape Character Assessment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Landscape Character Assessment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELandscape Character Assessment tells us what makes a place distinctive. It is a tool for identifying the features that give a locality its \u2018sense of place\u2019 and pinpointing what makes it different from its neighbouring areas. It provides a framework for describing an area in a systematic way.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "e1f07277-526d-4b7a-b079-9fd7e278c07a",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Layout"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Layout"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELayout refers to the spatial arrangement or organisation of various elements within a settlement. This includes the distribution of buildings, land uses, transportation networks, public spaces, infrastructure and amenities.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "3a388968-16e7-4ce2-886c-ec53b791c4fe",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Legibility"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Legibility"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELegibility refers to the clarity, coherence and ease of understanding of the spatial organisation and layout of a place. It involves how well the physical environment communicates information to people, allowing them to navigate, interpret and comprehend their surroundings effectively.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "8f4fc3f8-2b78-4221-802a-05728798fbcf",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Linear"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Linear"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ELinear typically refers to a spatial arrangement or feature that is elongated and extends in a straight or nearly straight line.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d3501441-97e5-4f7a-8d40-473b0f5d131d",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Listed building"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Listed building"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA listed building is a structure or building that has been officially designated as having special architectural, historical or cultural significance. There are three categories of listing in the UK: Grade I (buildings of exceptional interest), Grade II* (particularly important buildings of more than special interest) and Grade II (buildings of special interest).\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "013e21de-cd81-4e97-a0a3-628fd1e42cc4",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Local Planning Authority"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Local Planning Authority"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA Local Planning Authority is the public body responsible for managing and making decisions on planning matters within a defined area.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "758a020a-c4ed-4e9f-a265-f3691fc9f4a6",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "M4(2) accessible and adaptable dwellings"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "M4(2) accessible and adaptable dwellings"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EM4(2) is a standard for accessible and adaptable dwellings requiring step-free access, wider doorways, and features to allow for easy adaptation over time for people of all ages and abilities, including for toddlers with buggies, those with reduced mobility, or wheelchair users.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "5dca8674-4277-4c97-a371-ff83e0a6d183",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "M4(3) wheelchair accessible dwellings"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "M4(3) wheelchair accessible dwellings"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EM4(3) is a standard requirement where a new dwelling must provide reasonable provisions for a wheelchair user to live in the dwelling and have the ability to use any private outdoor space, parking and communal facilities.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d9b27ee3-cd6b-4301-804a-761033a3e709",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Major development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Major development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EMajor development refers to proposals involving 10 or more homes, housing on sites of 0.5 hectares or more, non-residential schemes creating 1,000m\u00B2 or more of floorspace, or developments on sites of 1 hectare or more.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f728bfcf-c671-4cf2-9c52-42a5fc46a82b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Massing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Massing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EMassing refers to the three-dimensional form, volume, and arrangement of building masses or structures within a built environment. It involves the overall shape, size, scale and configuration of buildings, as well as their relationship to each other and the surrounding environment.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "57d591d1-adb4-4523-8d7d-080ffd274106",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Material consideration"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Material consideration"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA material consideration is a factor that planning authorities may legally take into account when making decisions on planning applications or development proposals.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1c715ed3-a709-40b8-8cc1-3ced6a98fc83",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Micro-climate"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Micro-climate"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA micro-climate refers to the climate conditions that prevail within a relatively small or localised area, such as a garden, park, street or building courtyard.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "9ce8ac09-73ae-4767-8b7e-bcfd33b4b89f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Mixed use"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Mixed use"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EMixed use refers to the development of land that allows for multiple complementary land uses within a single area, building or development project.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "4dbb1724-882f-4efd-9874-72f55bd6334c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Modal filters"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Modal filters"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EModal filters are road management tools that allow some transportation modes, such as walking and cycling, while restricting others, typically motor vehicles, by blocking or diverting through-traffic. They are used to reduce traffic volume and speed, improve safety and air quality in residential areas, and encourage active travel. Common examples include physical barriers like bollards or planters, one-way street systems, bus gates, and sign-only restrictions.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "eafe2732-ec9d-4339-b2fd-5cca52017c6b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Movement network"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Movement network"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA movement network refers to a structured system or arrangement through which people move from one place to another.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f422dbdf-6a6f-4790-b2ea-0ee33f1af89a",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Natural surveillance"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Natural surveillance"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENatural surveillance is a concept in urban design and crime prevention that involves designing environments in a way that maximises visibility and observation of public spaces by residents, workers or passers-by.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "62d344a2-1fec-4b25-b862-8301dfd96377",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Neighbourhood plan"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Neighbourhood plan"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA plan prepared by a parish council or neighbourhood forum for a designated area which sets out policies and proposals for the development and use of land in that area.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d7b830d9-032c-472c-a3cf-59b2b14805fc",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Overbearing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Overbearing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA term used to describe the impact of a development or building on its surroundings, particularly a neighbouring property, in terms of its scale, massing, and general dominating effect.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "5181c006-b065-4f9e-9325-0bc6c1b6708c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Over development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Over development"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EAn amount of development that is excessive in terms of demands on infrastructure and services, or impact on local amenity and character.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f004ff50-6080-4d93-8e19-926fcd472932",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Passive surveillance"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Passive surveillance"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPassive surveillance refers to the design of built environments to enhance safety and security through passive means. It involves creating physical environments that encourage visibility, natural monitoring, and informal social control by residents, workers or other users of public spaces.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "054148de-551b-4192-9a59-da07dcc0a9e3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Patterning"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Patterning"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPatterning is the use of repetitive designs, shapes, and forms to create a visual or functional effect, like patterned bricks or tile layouts.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "07fc5472-7d2a-463a-8f5d-b2181186bf59",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Permeability"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Permeability"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPermeability refers to the ease with which people can move through an area or space. It is a measure of how accessible and navigable a place is, affecting both pedestrian and vehicular movement.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f03ad5a7-5c96-4220-a5ac-541e6ef69a85",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Permeable paving / surfacing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Permeable paving / surfacing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA hard surface that doesn\u2019t absorb water itself, but because it has small gaps or spaces in its pattern, rainwater can drain down through those gaps into the layer underneath, like concrete block paving.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d4ba63df-0b1d-4cf8-9a92-49775e82cb9e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Piers"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Piers"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA pier, in architecture, is an upright support for a structure or superstructure such as an arch or bridge. Sections of structural walls between openings (bays) can function as piers. External or free-standing walls may have piers at the ends or on corners.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "57f01a5a-f4e4-48e7-923a-f6a527ea5e8b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Placemaking"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Placemaking"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPlacemaking is an approach to planning, designing and managing public spaces that focuses on creating vibrant, engaging and inclusive environments. It involves transforming spaces into meaningful places that reflect the needs, values and culture of the community.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "22bfad66-7b20-44a6-aa94-189994c7323f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Plaza"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Plaza"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA plaza primarily refers to a public open space or square within a city, though it can also mean a shopping centre or a highway service area, depending on context.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "3ad82489-3f30-46eb-afa5-2d60db96fa7e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Pocket Park"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Pocket Park"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA pocket park is a small open space typically situated on a single plot or irregularly shaped plot of land within a built-up area.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "0c6b1a75-48da-49f6-a962-21eda13a568b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Priority habitats and species"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Priority habitats and species"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPriority habitats and species are those listed as Species and Habitats of Principal Importance on the England Biodiversity List, published by the Secretary of State under section 41 of the Natural Environment and Rural Communities Act 2006.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "006917b9-fac7-48eb-a377-07be9c939d73",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Projection"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Projection"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA physical feature or element of a building that extends beyond the primary enclosing walls, or a physical projection along the building line.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f933d120-dd24-47ca-a4fb-09c9c66f7033",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Public art"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Public art"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EArt that is located where the public have access or sight of it. Public art could be art or craft that is designed to celebrate, enliven or enrich a building, space or event.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1dd5c319-9e2d-4a4f-9c77-d3ac54d70b60",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Public realm"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Public realm"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EPublic realm refers to the spaces accessible and used by the general public in a settlement.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "e449d909-5487-455c-af39-42d4bcd5e5f5",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Quoin"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Quoin"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe external corner stones of a building, usually larger or differently finished than the surrounding masonry. Quoins reinforce the structure and add visual emphasis to corners.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "59a8b0b7-d681-429f-b8a9-7690256ddd75",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Radii / radius"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Radii / radius"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ERadii / radius refers to the line segment that extends from the centre of a circle or sphere to any point on its circumference or surface, measuring the distance between the centre and that point.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "d182ab25-76ab-4c2f-ab0e-445f861cb0b6",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Rain garden"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Rain garden"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA rain garden is a type of sustainable drainage system (SuDS). It typically consists of shallow depressions planted with native vegetation that can tolerate both wet and dry conditions.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "9c4e2a07-3f2f-462d-898f-1874a376e42d",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Rainwater harvesting"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Rainwater harvesting"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ERainwater harvesting is the process of collecting, storing and utilising rainwater that falls on roofs, pavements and other surfaces for various purposes, such as irrigation, landscaping and toilet flushing.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "94cb08ae-6b50-42ad-b3a2-0b288dbfbbe3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Recumbents"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Recumbents"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ERecumbent means lying down, reclining, or leaning, often in a position of comfort or rest. The term can also describe a type of bicycle, known as a recumbent bike, where the rider sits in a reclined position with their legs out in front.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ac720216-3776-454a-aa6a-b22255faf727",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Renewable and low carbon energy"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Renewable and low carbon energy"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ERenewable and low carbon energy refer to energy derived from natural resources that are replenished continuously or relatively quickly within human timescales. These sources of energy include sunlight, wind, water (hydropower), biomass and geothermal heat.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "99b9b619-c0de-47e8-b33d-6392769b1177",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Retrofitting"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Retrofitting"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ERetrofitting refers to the process of upgrading or modifying existing structures, systems, or components to improve their performance, efficiency, safety or functionality.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "c41ad4d7-e609-4cde-92cc-49e839a3d236",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Retention (trees)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Retention (trees)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ERetention for trees means preserving and keeping existing trees on a site, often during development, as required by planning conditions or local authorities. This practice aims to maintain their amenity value (aesthetic, environmental, and community benefits) and is determined through BS5837 tree surveys which categorise trees based on their quality and life expectancy.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "da91c541-7a60-49d2-9572-f05a6bfb4ff9",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Ridgeline"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Ridgeline"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA ridgeline refers to the horizontal line formed by the intersection of the highest points of a roof where two sloping roof planes meet at their peak.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "95d038d4-bd3f-486b-9e19-b8f09bb0b72e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Rockfaced Stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Rockfaced Stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStone that has a rough, natural-looking surface, typically achieved by chiselling or pitching. It gives a rugged, textured appearance and is often used for contrast or emphasis.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "75b9a0a9-8af9-413b-9f44-c266a6ac4272",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Scale"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Scale"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EScale refers to the relative size, proportion, and spatial dimensions of elements within the built environment, including buildings, streets, blocks and entire neighbourhoods.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "894eb02d-bedd-49b8-a781-de74bb09a831",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sense of place"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sense of place"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESense of place refers to the subjective, emotional and often deeply ingrained connection that individuals or communities feel towards a particular location or environment.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "8ad90f97-d9bf-446e-8afd-54a014e54f3c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Separation distances"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Separation distances"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESeparation distances refer to the minimum required space between new or extended dwellings and existing neighbouring properties to ensure adequate residential amenity, primarily through maintaining privacy and avoiding overshadowing.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "5cac1352-037c-435d-8099-453bc11d6586",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Serial vision"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Serial vision"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EIn planning and architecture, serial vision refers to the evolving, sequential visual experience of moving through a space, first coined by British architect Gordon Cullen. It\u0027s the idea that an urban environment is perceived not all at once, but as a series of \u0022revelations\u0022 where new details, contrasts, and perspectives unfold with each step, creating a dynamic and engaging journey for the viewer. \u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ea1c1565-ad80-466a-b48b-6681518994fc",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Shared spaces"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Shared spaces"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStreets designed so that vehicles \u2018naturally\u2019 give way to pedestrians - typically the separation between carriageway and footway is reduced and the difference between the zone where vehicles are permitted and the area designated for pedestrians is less physically distinct than in a conventional street.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "dea173c6-d85a-420d-85fd-e66ee47df3c9",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Soft landscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Soft landscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESoft landscape refers to the use of natural elements within outdoor spaces to enhance their aesthetic appeal, functionality and environmental quality.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "8be3b1ca-0f3f-45a4-972a-a1088f789135",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Squared Stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Squared Stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStone that has been cut or dressed into square or rectangular shapes with straight edges. Squared stone allows for tight joints and a more refined finish in masonry.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "44e8f144-a6f3-4a6f-b0a3-00287300b225",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Staggered (building line)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Staggered (building line)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EBuildings can be staggered and at varying distances from the road to create more diverse, interesting streetscapes and public spaces, especially in suburban or lower-density areas, by breaking up monotonous lines and allowing for varied building sizes and public-private transitions. This design approach often prioritises a sense of place and character by creating a more informal, \u0022organic\u0022 layout that can also accommodate local conditions and desired aesthetic outcomes, such as urban density or a more rural feel.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "a69fd737-ae39-4f9b-8022-b1cfc00a3b91",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Stakeholder"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Stakeholder"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA stakeholder is any individual, group, organisation or entity that has a vested interest, concern or influence in a particular outcome. Typical stakeholders in development projects can include government agencies, local authorities, members of the community and the private sector.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "145aefe1-606a-47e0-867f-06dde7f53812",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Strategic (requirements)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Strategic (requirements)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStrategic requirements refer to the broad goals and priorities that guide long-term development across a region, such as housing needs, transport links, and healthcare provision, identified through strategic planning to connect and coordinate activity across multiple sectors and local authorities to achieve a unified vision for a future area.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "977d4662-8668-4ed0-8e78-67761400c3c3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Streetscene / streetscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Streetscene / streetscape"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStreetscene / streetscape refers to the visual appearance, character, and overall design of a street or roadway, including its physical elements, architectural features, landscaping and street furniture.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "3217372d-1b71-4560-8e78-4c4a17be4a21",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Street furniture"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Street furniture"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStreet furniture refers to a variety of functional and aesthetic objects installed along streets, pavements, and other public spaces to enhance the comfort, convenience, safety and visual appeal of urban environments. Key examples of street furniture include benches and seating, bins, cycle storage, bus shelters, streetlights, signage, planters and tree guards, public art installations and wayfinding markers.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "9b303848-a95d-41c0-b9d2-d69a4ef8c372",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Street hierarchy"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Street hierarchy"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA street hierarchy is a classification system that categorises streets and roadways into distinct types or classes based on their function, design, capacity and importance within the overall transportation network.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "4c6f296e-0edb-4a90-b76f-83e07ee3ce0a",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Supplementary Planning Document (SPD)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Supplementary Planning Document (SPD)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESupplementary planning documents (SPDs) should build upon and provide more detailed advice or guidance on policies in an adopted local plan.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "bc53d2e4-124b-419c-a469-5b2e0e1745e5",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Surface water runoff"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Surface water runoff"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESurface water runoff refers to the movement of rainwater, snowmelt, or other precipitation over the land surface, eventually flowing into streams, rivers, lakes or oceans. It occurs when precipitation exceeds the infiltration capacity of the soil or when the ground is saturated.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "a1a45b42-dd4c-468f-b51e-9455398aefba",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sustainability"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sustainability"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESustainability refers to the ability to meet the needs of the present generation without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs. It involves balancing economic, environmental, and social considerations to ensure that human activities are conducted in a way that preserves natural resources, minimises negative impacts on ecosystems and communities and promotes long-term well-being and resilience.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "e082ee7e-ce6e-48a6-ab16-d34d77c10a3c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sustainable drainage systems (SuDS)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sustainable drainage systems (SuDS)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESustainable drainage systems (SuDS) are innovative approaches to managing surface water runoff in built areas in a more environmentally friendly and sustainable manner.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1ce9228f-a024-427f-964f-a95924cf3b38",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sustainable transport modes"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Sustainable transport modes"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ESustainable transport modes are efficient, safe and accessible ways to travel with minimal environmental impact, including walking, cycling, ultra-low and zero emission vehicles, car sharing and public transport.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "984c403f-0ce2-45dc-975d-f57329f60c3f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Swale"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Swale"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA swale is a type of sustainable drainage system (SuDS). It is a shallow, vegetated depression or low-lying area designed to manage surface water runoff by temporarily storing, infiltrating or conveying stormwater in a controlled manner.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "197815dc-0ab8-48b6-9dc2-43f0249ab45b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tactile paving"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tactile paving"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ETactile paving consists of a pattern of raised or textured surfaces installed on pedestrian walkways, train platforms, or other public spaces to assist individuals with visual impairments or mobility disabilities in navigating safely and independently.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "9c288ac5-1ffa-48c9-ad36-8012e4ca6bf3",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tooled Stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tooled Stone"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStone that has been worked with tools to create a specific surface texture or pattern, such as parallel lines or a smooth finish. Tooling can be decorative or used to match historic finishes.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "4e9214a8-eb55-4ef0-aed5-a58cdf6d2b8f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Topography"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Topography"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe arrangement of the natural and man-made physical features of an area.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "777e44c7-9236-4983-9c0e-98e8ced69d19",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Transport assessment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Transport assessment"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA transport assessment is a detailed process that evaluates transport issues linked to a proposed development. It identifies measures to encourage alternatives to car travel, improve accessibility and safety, and manage the expected transport impacts.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "228bf8f1-27a7-4aaf-8125-cd7aae852138",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Transport statement"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Transport statement"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA transport statement is a simplified report used when transport issues from a development are limited, and a full transport assessment is unnecessary.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "b5ca38ff-c49c-4064-aa03-c41812e26e9c",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Travel plan"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Travel plan"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA travel plan is a long-term strategy for an organisation or site setting out how sustainable transport goals will be achieved, monitored and regularly updated.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "02ab15dc-21ad-4e8a-95c8-4fd7f088a5a5",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tree pit"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Tree pit"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA tree pit is an excavated area in the ground specifically designed to accommodate the planting and growth of trees in built environments.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "fa5f4e9e-242d-4587-ba95-515e9cad83f4",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Trees and Design Action Group (TDAG) Database"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Trees and Design Action Group (TDAG) Database"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe Trees and Design Action Group (TDAG) is a collaborative initiative focused on promoting the integration of trees and green infrastructure into urban planning, design and development practices.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "abec69fd-be4f-4aa6-80f6-0ee3fb813a7e",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "UPVC"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "UPVC"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EUPVC stands for unplasticised polyvinyl chloride. It is a type of plastic that is commonly used in the building and construction industry, particularly for window frames, doors and piping.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "ce401221-141e-4e51-b085-d73d2012ea20",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Urban grain"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Urban grain"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EUrban grain refers to the characteristics that define the pattern, scale and texture of built form within a built area. It encompasses the arrangement, density and diversity of buildings, streets, blocks and open spaces that collectively shape the physical fabric of built environments.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "afb2df0f-1ce5-4a45-84d1-85930cea5f96",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Vehicles per day (vpd)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Vehicles per day (vpd)"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EVehicles per day (vpd) is a traffic volume measure of the average number of vehicles that use a specific road section in a 24-hour period, indicating how busy that road is. It is a fundamental traffic data point used in various applications, including traffic impact studies for developments, assessing infrastructure investments, and providing data for traffic modelling and planning.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "9505eb26-185b-40bd-ad1b-893be233abd8",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Verge"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Verge"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EVerge refers to the edge, border or limit of something. It is commonly used to refer to a strip of land at the side of a road or pavement.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "1c0875bc-4c13-44e0-a434-c9ec4a47d9d8",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Vertical \u0027hit and miss\u0027 timber fencing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Vertical \u0027hit and miss\u0027 timber fencing"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EVertical hit and miss timber fence is a decorative, slatted fence where vertical timber boards are alternately fixed to the front and back of the supporting posts, creating a pattern of gaps that are both stylish and allow wind to pass through. This design provides a semi-solid look that is appealing from both sides of the fence, making it a good option for shared boundaries and windy locations. \u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "f2e90d48-716b-467b-9f4d-2dd59a17fb01",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "View / vista"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "View / vista"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA view / vista refers to a visual perspective or sightline from a specific vantage point typically encompassing views of natural or built features such as landscapes, landmarks, buildings, public spaces and streetscapes.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "05788565-db4a-400a-b4a3-8dbe4636d901",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Wayfinding"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Wayfinding"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EWayfinding is the process of orientating and navigating through an environment, typically unfamiliar or complex, to reach desired destinations efficiently and effectively.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "2ddfeed5-de84-4740-a597-1d6bbbea144f",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EWetlands are transitional ecosystems where water is the primary factor determining the nature of the soil and the types of plant and animal communities present.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Wetlands"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Wetlands"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "3e535bb6-3999-49a3-8844-b5f00645f3f4",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Wildlife corridor or network"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Wildlife corridor or network"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EA wildlife corridor or network refers to a connected system of natural habitats that facilitates the movement, dispersal and genetic exchange of wildlife populations within a landscape.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "64b4e1d1-ed6f-40ae-bca9-144d77e37189",
      "key": "989c95b0-45c2-4483-aecf-ef4847fa4ae8",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "References and Bibliography"
        },
        {
          "alias": "anchorName",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "References and Bibliography"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch4\u003EActive Design Guidance (2023)\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Active Design Guidance was produced by Sport England to encourage the integration of physical activity opportunities into the planning, design and management of built environments to promote active and healthy lifestyles.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EBuilding for a Healthy Life (2020)\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBuilding for a Healthy Life was produced by Homes England and sets out national design principles and guidance developed to promote the creation of healthy, sustainable and inclusive communities through urban planning and development.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EThe Building Regulations 2010\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Building Regulations 2010 are UK legislation relating to the construction and extension of buildings in the UK. Building regulations approval is separate from planning permission and both may be required.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EThe Building Regulations 2010, Sewerage Sector Guidance\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Building Regulations, Sewerage Sector Guidance refers to the regulations provided within the Building Regulations 2010 relating to the design, installation and maintenance of sewerage systems in buildings and developments.\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EBuilding with Nature Green Infrastructure Standards Framework\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Building with Nature Green Infrastructure Standards Framework was produced by Building with Nature and provides nature-based solutions in the planning, design, construction and management of built environments to enhance resilience, sustainability and human well-being.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ECycle Infrastructure Design Local Transport Note 1/20 (2020)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Cycle Infrastructure Design Local Transport Note was produced by the Department of Transport and provides guidance and good practice for the design of cycle infrastructure, in support of the Cycling and Walking Investment Strategy.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EDesign Manual for Roads and Bridges (2020)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Design Manual for Roads and Bridges was produced by National Highways and contains information about design standards relating to the design, assessment and operation of motorway and all-purpose trunk roads in the UK.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EDesign of Pedestrian Crossings Local Transport Note 2/95 (1995)\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Design of Pedestrian Crossings is a Local Transport Note produced by the Department for Transport that recommends the practices to be followed when planning, designing and installing at-grade pedestrian crossings.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EEnvironment Act 2021\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Environment Act 2021 is UK legislation enacted to address a range of environmental challenges, set long-term environmental goals, and establish mechanisms for environmental protection, restoration and improvement.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EThe Future Homes Standard (emerging)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Future Homes Standard (FHS) will complement the Building Regulations 2010 and aims to ensure that new homes built from 2025 produce 75-80% less carbon emissions than homes delivered under the existing regulations.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EGreen Infrastructure Framework (2023)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Green Infrastructure Framework is a strategic initiative produced by Natural England aimed at promoting and enhancing green infrastructure across England.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ECycle Infrastructure Design Local Transport Note 1/20 (2020)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Green Infrastructure Planning and Design Guide is a component of Natural England\u2019s Green Infrastructure Framework and aims to provide practical, evidence-based advice on how to plan, design, deliver and manage good quality green infrastructure that helps to create beautiful nature-rich places.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EInterim Code of Practice for Sustainable Drainage Systems (2004)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Interim Code of Practice for Sustainable Drainage Systems was produced by the National SUDS Working Group and provides a strategic approach to the allocation of maintenance for sustainable drainage systems in England and Wales.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ELevelling-up and Regeneration Act 2023\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Levelling-up and Regeneration Act 2023 is UK legislation aiming to ensure that new development is built beautifully, produces more local infrastructure, is shaped by local people\u2019s democratic wishes, enhances the environment and creates neighbourhoods where people want to live and work.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EManual for Streets (2007)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EManual for Streets was produced by the Department for Transport and provides best practice advice on the design, planning and management of streets and urban spaces. It aims to promote a more people-centred approach to street design that prioritises the needs of pedestrians, cyclists and other vulnerable road users, while also accommodating the safe and efficient movement of vehicles.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ENational Design Guide (NDG) (2021)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe National Design Guide (NDG) was produced by the Department for Levelling Up, Housing and Communities (now the Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government) and includes a set of design principles and recommendations to inform the planning, design and development of the built environment across England.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ENational Model Design Code (NMDC) (2021)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe National Model Design Code (NMDC) was produced by the Department for Levelling Up, Housing and Communities (now the Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government) and serves as a valuable resource for promoting high-quality design outcomes, fostering consistency and coherence in the built environment and advancing sustainable and inclusive development practices at the national, regional and local levels.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ENational Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (2024)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) was produced by the Ministry of Housing, Communities and Local Government and sets out the planning policies and guidelines for England. It provides a framework for local planning authorities to use when preparing their local development plans and making decisions on planning applications.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ENational Standards for Sustainable Drainage Systems (SuDS) (2025)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe national standards provide information for designers, property developers, local authorities and other interested parties, such as sewerage undertakers and the Environment Agency. They also contain links to additional supporting information relating to sustainable drainage systems (SuDS).\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EGuidance for Outdoor Sport and Play: Beyond the Six Acre Standard (2020)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EGuidance for Outdoor Sport and Play: Beyond the Six Acre Standard emphasises the need for a range of both formal and informal outdoor spaces to meet our recreational\u0026nbsp;needs and the practical tools to guarantee sufficient space is available. The guidance is for practitioners, local planning authorities, developers, planners, urban designers, landscape architects and parish and town councils, in the planning and design of outdoor sport, play and informal open space.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EPlanning Practice Guidance (2023)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPlanning Practice Guidance refers to the National Planning Policy Framework and its associated planning practice guidance.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EStreets and Transport in the Urban Environment Guidelines (2014-2019)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Streets and Transport in the Urban Environment Guidelines were produced by the Chartered Institution of Highways and Transportation and include a range of guidelines relating to buses in urban developments, creating better streets, designing for walking and planning for cycling.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EThe Road to Zero (2018)\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Road to Zero is the UK Government\u2019s strategy setting out the steps towards cleaner road transport and delivering an industrial strategy.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ESecured by Design\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESecured by Design is the official police security initiative that works to improve the security of buildings and their immediate surroundings to provide safe places to live, work, shop and visit.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EStreet Improvement Manual (2020)\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Street Improvement Manual was produced by the Urban Design Group and provides local authorities with ideas and assistance in transforming their streets so that they are safe for pedestrians and cyclists of all ages and abilities and support the social and economic life of the community.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch4\u003ETraffic Signs Manual (2022)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe Traffic Signs Manual was produced by the Department for Transport and gives guidance on the use of traffic signs and road markings in the UK prescribed by the Traffic Signs Regulations.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
